checks_run.procedure:
Run the no-CDN check, then my own scan of the P4 diff d3e6fe6..a91d82c (apps, packages). The scan looks for:
- secret-like assignments (D4);
- remote URLs (D5);
- dynamic code (D6);
- sql.raw and sql.lit (D7, D12);
- innerHTML (D8);
- float arithmetic on money (D9).

checks_run.actual:
91 writes were captured across 42 operations. 35 of them, across 23 operations, have foreign ids in the body; examples are createTraceLink, createInheritedRecord, createBauHandover, createBenefitOverlap, createChangeRequest, requestApproval and previewChangeImpact.

All 35 replays were refused:
- 15 × 422 validation.reference;
- 4 × 422 trace_link.record_not_found;
- 5 × 400;
- 3 × 404;
- 2 × 422 inherited_record.not_modular;
- 2 × 422 approval.decision_right_unknown;
- one each of 403 champion_constraint.not_champion, 422 gate.*, risk_disposition.not_open_risk and stakeholder_group.kpi_invalid.

The foreign checksum is unchanged; 2/2 passed, exit 0. inherited_record also has the 0055 composite FKs to the same transformation (ADR-0038 §7.1).

36 residual routes, all resolved:
- local openWrite atCommit closures in kpi actuals, versions and trajectories;
- lockForWrite or openSustainmentWrite chains in budget, milestones and handovers;
- the gate-exception and portfolio-link factories;
- one read sent as POST (previewChangeImpact);
- P1 organization and transformation routes, and the P2 register kit.

Every write route of a P4 operation reaches a commit-time re-check. Three DG2 product-gate operations that P4 extends (decideGate, submitGate, updateGate) authorize on the request-start grants: F-DG4-103, Low, not mandatory.

The I/O grep finds nothing in P4 server code.

